source: nexus.lib.node-export
payload:
  status: REAL
  source: >-
    lib/gate-walker.js walks a step_chain: an ordered set of steps, each a gate. The chain is the stepwise surface a drone,
    a person or copilot advances — James, 2026-10-26: "each gate can be a step, like a question, then holds the data … use
    the gates as the surface." It reuses the gate-memory record (schema.gate, references not copies) to hold each step's
    result, phase-plan (GW24) + context-builder to hand each step only its budgeted packet, and raid-port + route-eligibility
    to route each step to its own agent. The chain GROWS as it runs: a step may decompose into sub-steps appended to it
    (dynamic decomposition). A step whose run reads outside its packet is a gap (§1.2), never hidden.
  fields:
    id:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: the chain's scope id — one chain per scope (a repo, a run, a session, a task)
    steps:
      type: array
      required: true
      description: >-
        ordered steps; each a gate. A step has: id (unique in the chain); kind (ask | act | check);
        depends_on (step ids that must be recorded PASSED/ANSWERED before this one is ready — the order);
        needs (the inputs this step reads, by reference: prior step ids and/or external ref ids — what bounds its packet);
        params (step-kind params: an ask's question; an act's task + the needs route-eligibility reads; a check's step-gate step name)
    created_by:
      type: string
      required: false
      description: who authored the chain (a person, copilot, a decomposer) — provenance, not authority
